      "text": "**\n\nFirst, let's convert the given spherical coordinates $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ into rectangular coordinates $\\left( x,y,z \\right)$.\n\nThe spherical to rectangular conversion formulas are:\n\n$ x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta$\n$ y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta$\n$ z = \\rho \\cos \\phi$\n\nGiven the spherical coordinates $( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 )$:\n\nStep 1: Convert $\\phi$:\nSince $\\phi = 0$, we can use the identity $\\cos(0) = 1$. Thus, $\\cos \\phi = 1$.\n\nStep 2: Convert $x$:\nUsing the formula $x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta$, we get:\n$x = 3 \\cdot \\sin(0)\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right)$\n\nSince $\\sin(0)$ equals 0, $x$ becomes:\n$x = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$.\n\nStep 3: Convert $y$:\nSimilarly, for $y$, we use $y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta$:\n$y = 3\\sin(0)\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right)$\n\nAgain, since $\\sin(0)$ equals 0, $y$ becomes:\n$y = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$.\n\nStep 4: Convert $z$:\nFinally, for $z$, given the spherical coordinate $\\phi = 0$, we have:\n$z = 3 \\cdot \\cos(0) = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3$.\n\nStep 5: Combine all the steps into the rectangular coordinates:\n$(x, y, z) = \\left( 0, 0, 3 \\right)$.\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates for the given spherical coordinates are $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ is $\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}$.",
